{"type":"record","name":"PressureFrame","namespace":"com.optionsedge.contracts.optionpressure","doc":"One published frame of the option pressure register, for a single strike or for a symbol. This is a DESCRIPTIVE surface: it names what the aggregated exposure-weighted residual flow currently looks like over each declared window, and it carries no forecast. actionable is false in every frame the producer can construct - the register was rejected on two gate sets and a directional validation over a year of SPXW sessions found no directional content - so a consumer may describe a frame but must not act on one.","fields":[{"name":"semanticLayer","type":"string","doc":"PRESSURE_STATE. Present so a reader can refuse a record from another layer rather than infer the layer from the topic."},{"name":"symbol","type":"string"},{"name":"expiry","type":"string"},{"name":"strike","type":"string","doc":"The strike for a strike-granularity frame, or the literal SYMBOL for the symbol-granularity frame. The two granularities run under DIFFERENT configurations - see implementedPressureConfigHash - so the value is part of the frame's identity, not a label."},{"name":"sessionId","type":"string"},{"name":"asOfEventTimeMs","type":"long","doc":"Event time of the input that produced this frame, never wall clock."},{"name":"pressureState","type":"string","doc":"INSUFFICIENT_DATA | NEUTRAL | CALL_PRESSURE | PUT_PRESSURE | UNUSABLE, after hysteresis and the persistence requirement. CALL_PRESSURE and PUT_PRESSURE are measured tail states: at symbol granularity the entry threshold is the 95th percentile of |level| over 5,504,676 GOOD seconds of the historical corpus, so they are rare by construction."},{"name":"qualityState","type":"string","doc":"GOOD | DEGRADED | UNUSABLE. GOOD means every declared quality floor was met for the primary window."},{"name":"qualityReasons","type":{"type":"array","items":"string"},"doc":"Why the quality is what it is, in declaration order; the single element NONE when nothing was wrong. Some reasons are sticky for the session once raised, so this is a record of the session's integrity rather than of this instant."},{"name":"windows","type":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"record","name":"PressureWindowView","fields":[{"name":"horizonMs","type":"long","doc":"Exact rolling duration in milliseconds; zero denotes the session-to-date window."},{"name":"level","type":["null","double"],"doc":"The aggregate, null when the window holds no admissible mass. Null is NOT zero: zero is balanced flow and null is no observation.","default":null},{"name":"mass","type":"double"},{"name":"rawCount","type":"long","doc":"Prints seen. Larger than blockCount whenever several prints shared one one-second block, which is the de-autocorrelation this register applies."},{"name":"blockCount","type":"long","doc":"One-second information blocks, the register's actual sample count."},{"name":"effectiveSamples","type":"double","doc":"Kish effective sample size of the weighted blocks, which is what the minimum-samples floor is judged on."},{"name":"coverageRatio","type":"double"},{"name":"trueSpanMs","type":"long","doc":"Span actually covered, which is shorter than horizonMs while the window is still filling."},{"name":"finalized","type":"boolean"}]}},"doc":"One view per declared window, in configured order. A reader picks a window by horizonMs and never by position."},{"name":"includedCount","type":"long"},{"name":"excludedCount","type":"long"},{"name":"unknownAggressorCount","type":"long"},{"name":"modelVersion","type":"string","doc":"The upstream residual model this frame was built from."},{"name":"opbConfigHash","type":"string","doc":"Identity of the upstream residual configuration."},{"name":"implementedPressureConfigHash","type":"string","doc":"Identity of the TEN pressure-register fields this producer implements, NOT the wider pressureConfigHash of the design. Named apart on purpose: emitting a subset under the registered name would misdirect attribution. It differs between the strike and symbol granularities and it rotates stored state when it changes."},{"name":"actionable","type":"boolean","doc":"Always false. The producing record refuses to construct a frame with it set, so a true value here cannot have come from this service."}]}